In this case, I believe my original comments are merited.  I did notice the blurry movement (increase the shutter speed and/or ISO to eliminate that) and that the composition is tight on the feet (provide more breathing room at time of capture for adjustments).  Sure ... it is a pretty photo, but that does not mean it is perfect.

